#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The Gobelin Hurlant pictures, generated by the local ComfyUI, gently: the machine is shared.

    python3 tools/gobelin_images.py takes              # style takes, into RAW/takes
    python3 tools/gobelin_images.py make [name ...]    # the site's pictures, into RAW
    python3 tools/gobelin_images.py ship               # RAW to gobelin/img, resized, as .webp

One image at a time, each under the GPU flock the parallax tools use, and only with RESERVE_MB
of memory free: it waits rather than push the box over. ComfyUI itself is started and stopped by
whoever runs this: nice -n 15 python main.py, stopped after the batch. Raw PNGs stay out of
the repo, in RAW; what ships is what `ship` writes. The seeds are the ones kept, but capture, bureau
and cave were painted before GOBLIN was sharpened: a rerun gives a sibling, not the same picture.

A picture never carries text from the model: its lettering is always false. What must be read
(the whiteboard, a clue) is pasted on by `ship`.
"""
